# Codex workflow reference

## Session defaults (last verified 2026-09-15)

- Plain `codex` starts with `{{ .agents.codex.defaults.model }}` at {{ .agents.codex.defaults.model_reasoning_effort }} reasoning effort; plan mode is
  pinned to {{ .agents.codex.defaults.plan_mode_reasoning_effort }}. `review_model` and `[agents] default_subagent_model` are managed
  to `{{ .subagent_tiers.codex.top }}`, so `/review` and unpinned children run the top worker tier.
- `/model` changes the model or reasoning effort for the current session only; a
  new session returns to the managed defaults. `/fast` is a separate speed
  toggle, not a model or reasoning-effort profile.
- No launch profiles and no persisted mode override: start with plain `codex`
  and make plan-mode or other temporary changes per session in the TUI.

## Limits (last verified 2026-09-10; revisit Sol pricing 2026-11-21, the context window at the next Codex CLI catalog bump)

- Metering is token-based credits (since 2026-04): one pool shared across CLI,
  IDE extension, cloud tasks and other ChatGPT agent surfaces, drawn on a weekly
  window plus a rolling 5-hour window — both potentially binding; check `/status`.
{{ includeTemplate "openai-rate-card.md" . -}}
- Compare successful-task cost including reasoning, cached context, retries and
  delegation; a larger model can use fewer tokens without being cheaper. Keep
  bounded work on the lower tiers, Fast off unless needed, and drop reasoning
  effort per session via `/model` for routine work — effort scales burn directly.
- Child agents draw the same credit pool as the parent, scaling roughly linearly
  with concurrent subagents at equal model/effort (OpenAI engineer,
  openai/codex#13179), so delegation saves credits only when children run
  cheaper models or lower effort — #32587 below can silently void that.
{{ includeTemplate "openai-context-window.md" . -}}
- Do not raise `model_context_window` above it: Codex clamps to the catalog's
  `max_context_window` and then to ~95%, so a larger number is cosmetic
  (`/status` shows it until the first message, then the real cap) and it
  miscalibrates auto-compaction, which is sized off the configured window.
- Attached MCP servers reload their full tool schemas every turn — an accepted
  cost here; revisit the server list if the weekly limit starts binding.

## Subagents (last verified 2026-07-31 — unverified since; re-verify from a Codex session)

- Named specialists under `~/.codex/agents` stay pinned to their configured
  model tier, even after `/model` changes the parent session.
- Known upstream regression (openai/codex#32587, MultiAgent V2; still open
  2026-09-12, last upstream activity 2026-07-12): spawned subagents can silently
  inherit the parent's model/effort instead of their pinned config. After Codex
  CLI updates, verify a specialist ran its pin via `/status` or the session log
  before trusting tier economics — doubly so under an Astra parent (2.5× Sol).
- `implementer` (added 2026-08-28; remit widened 2026-09-21): mid-tier (Terra)
  executor for any bounded slice of a settled design, mechanical or substantive
  — weighted credit rates make it far cheaper than inline edits in a grown
  session, and #32587 erases exactly that economics.
- OpenAI's Codex guidance routes read-heavy exploration subagents to Terra; the
  small tier here stays on Luna (bounded extraction-shaped presets, far cheaper)
  — revisit if explorer output quality disappoints.

## Waiting on children (last verified 2026-09-21, codex-cli 0.154.0)

- `wait_agent` is event-driven: it returns as soon as any child finishes, a
  child messages the parent, or I type — `timeout_ms` is only the ceiling
  (upstream min 10 s, default 30 s, max 1 h), so a long wait costs nothing.
- A finished child does not wake a parent that has ended its turn
  (openai/codex#46120, open): block in `wait_agent`, never end the turn to wait.
- `features.multi_agent_v2.{min,default}_wait_timeout_ms` are managed to 5 min,
  so shorter requests are clamped up; the built-in "prefer longer waits" hint
  did not stop 10 s polling. Reverse when #46120 ships or a stalled child makes
  a 5-minute block hurt.

## Command output (last verified 2026-09-21, codex-cli 0.154.0)

- `exec_command` returns at `yield_time_ms` with whatever output exists; a
  result carrying a `session_id` is still running, and its empty output is not
  a pass — collect the exit code with `write_stdin` before reporting a check.

## Frontier driver (decision 2026-09-15)

- The frontier tier `{{ .subagent_tiers.codex.frontier }}` is the session default (shared `frontier_driver`
  rule in AGENTS.md); specialist pins are unchanged and no child runs it. There is
  no blocking lever: `SubagentStart` receives only the agent type and "`continue:
  false` doesn't stop the subagent", so pins are defaults, not guarantees — run
  the #32587 pin check after each CLI update.
- Availability depends on the account and installed harness. A model catalog
  entry is not proof of account access; never substitute another provider or
  paid API routing when subscription access is unavailable.
